                            <comment id="502326" author="gerrit" created="Mon, 28 Sep 2026 14:52:36 +0000">&lt;p&gt;"Chakshu Kansal &amp;lt;ckansal@ddn.com&amp;gt;" uploaded a new patch: &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69287" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69287&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Subject: &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20755" title="sanity-sec interop issues with 2.16 server" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20755"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20755&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; tests: fix sanity-sec/5 and sanity-sec/64a for older servers&lt;br/&gt;
Project: fs/lustre-release&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Current Patch Set: 1&lt;br/&gt;
Commit: 898b31df14508111c42dd70d2b861ea0e5a37720&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="502331" author="JIRAUSER19503" created="Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:40:02 +0000">&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;test_5 was introduced by "&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19996" title="l_getidentity produces improper logs" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19996"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19996&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; utils: Make l_getidentity produce proper errno", which is not present in the b2_16 branch. As a result, the expected errno is different on b2_16 servers.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;test_64a, on b2_16, setting the project ID with &lt;b&gt;lfs project -p&lt;/b&gt; requires the projid_set RBAC role now.&lt;br/&gt;
For the master client running against an older 2.16 server, the test must not request the projid_set role. This role is not supported by the older server, so nodemap_modify rejects the entire RBAC value with EINVAL.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Tests 45, 47, 48b, and 49 are showing timeout failures during interop testing with the 2.16 server.&lt;br/&gt;
The failures appear to have some common LNet and bulk I/O errors, including the client being unable to reach the OSS. However, more investigation is needed to confirm whether they share the same root cause and determine the appropriate fix.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="504453" author="JIRAUSER19503" created="Tue, 27 Oct 2026 06:46:28 +0000">&lt;p&gt;The remaining test failures (45 47 48b 49) are potentially being addressed by &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20770" title="interop sanity-pfl,sanityn: Request sent has failed due to network error" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20770"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20770&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. I’ve rebased a debug patch to identify the remaining failures:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68576" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68576&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Tests test_5 and test_64a have already been fixed in a separate patch (yet to land). Failures should only include these tests for now.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
